From 5685947d52dec89063b28c4259fe2ac6021ceb61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:58:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 70/73] apps: Gives wlmmixer preferences, and leaves the right
 button to wlmaker.

wlmaker opens the dock-app's menu on a right-click, which offers muting and
the mixer application. A middle click still starts the mixer application.

wlmmixer reads its preferences file, and applies changes right away:
- Theme: The shared color themes, or its own colors.
- ShowPercent: Whether to show the volume in percent.
- ClickMutes: Whether a left click (not on the meter) toggles mute.
- ScrollVolume: Whether the mouse wheel changes the volume.
- Step, MaxVolume: As the commandline options, which remain defaults.
- MixerCommand: The mixer application; --mixer_command is the default.

The command is started through wlm_settings_spawn, shared by the DockApps.
